  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Born in Rome into a film-producing family, De Laurentiis formed Filmauro with his father Luigi in 1975. The company combined production and distribution with a chain of Roman cinemas. Its catalogue ranged from Italian comedies to international work by directors including Ridley Scott, David Lynch and Woody Allen. De Laurentiis also created the long-running cycle of Italian Christmas comedies and led the international federation of film producers.\n\nFootball became a second major enterprise when he acquired Napoli after bankruptcy in 2004. The club returned from the third tier to Serie A within three seasons, established itself in European competition and later won two league championships under his presidency. Filmauro also acquired the sporting rights of Bari, making it the company’s second Italian football club.",
    "html": "<p>Born in Rome into a film-producing family, De Laurentiis formed Filmauro with his father Luigi in 1975. The company combined production and distribution with a chain of Roman cinemas. Its catalogue ranged from Italian comedies to international work by directors including Ridley Scott, David Lynch and Woody Allen. De Laurentiis also created the long-running cycle of Italian Christmas comedies and led the international federation of film producers.</p>\r\n<p>Football became a second major enterprise when he acquired Napoli after bankruptcy in 2004. The club returned from the third tier to Serie A within three seasons, established itself in European competition and later won two league championships under his presidency. Filmauro also acquired the sporting rights of Bari, making it the company’s second Italian football club.</p>\r\n",
